Parent: 

To design a group-fair count-min sketch that is also group-fair, we propose two approaches based on the following observation: if elements from different groups do not collide with each other in the same row of the sketch, then their frequency estimates are guaranteed to be equal. In this section, 
Parent: 

We will design a Group-Fair Count-Min (FCM) sketch that satisfies Definition 2 and provides an approximation factor of at most $\epsilon$ for all groups g1andg 2. The price of fairness is the number of rows in the sketch. We show that our group-aware semi-uniform hash schemes are optimal, up to a constant factor, with respect to the additive error bound (Theorem 4).

To achieve this goal, we first introduce two notions: 
1) Group Fairness: A CM is called group-fair if it satisfies Definition 2. Specifically, for any element type from g1andg 2, its frequency estimate by the sketch is bounded by a constant factor of all other groups (Definition 2). In our case, we consider two binary groups g1andg 2for\nexplicating Parent:
